content:
This run is already one project. Do not list, rank, or select among registered projects.

Project id: {{project.id}}
Hub spoke: {{project.hub_root}}
Knowledge root: {{project.knowledge_root}}

Read the MCP resource see:/projects. Find the project whose id equals {{project.id}}. Its spokes array is the registered spoke list. Each entry has name and path. Do not invent spokes from directory names. If that project is missing, or spokes is missing, fail and do not return a manifest.

Inspect the hub spoke and every spoke in that array. Walk meaningful source and configuration. Ignore build output, dependencies, and vendor trees. Existing documentation is not evidence that a component still exists. Existing component records may be read only to keep a stable name for the same boundary.

Define components by responsibility and interface, not one directory per component. Include a hub-owned component when it has its own role. Each component has a unique lowercase kebab-case name, one owned_by spoke from the registered list, consumed_by as registered spoke names, a short present-tense role, and evidence paths that exist under the owner.

If any registered spoke cannot be inspected, the final stdout line is one JSON object with scan_complete false, spokes_inspected [], component_names [], and components []. On success the final stdout line is one JSON object with scan_complete true, spokes_inspected (the registered spoke names), component_names (string array), and components (array of objects with name, owned_by, consumed_by, role, evidence). component_names and components are the same set in the same order. Do not use a markdown fence.
